1
00:00:02,201 --> 00:00:06,243
Yuuji Itadori, by law I will
now exorcize you as a curse.

2
00:00:08,077 --> 00:00:09,702
(dramatic orchestral music)

3
00:00:09,785 --> 00:00:11,869
No, really, I'm feeling fine.

4
00:00:11,952 --> 00:00:13,136
Besides, you and I are
both pretty beat up.

5
00:00:13,160 --> 00:00:15,201
Shouldn't we see a doctor?

6
00:00:17,077 --> 00:00:18,261
[Fushiguro] I can't tell
if this is Itadori speaking

7
00:00:18,285 --> 00:00:20,410
or the cursed object.

8
00:00:21,577 --> 00:00:23,327
Dammit, what do I do now?

9
00:00:23,410 --> 00:00:25,077
[Satoru] What's the situation?

10
00:00:25,160 --> 00:00:27,368
Huh, Satoru Gojou?

11
00:00:27,452 --> 00:00:28,201
What are you doing here?

12
00:00:28,285 --> 00:00:29,328
Hey.

13
00:00:29,411 --> 00:00:31,995
I wasn't planning on showing up,

14
00:00:32,078 --> 00:00:34,911
but you got kind
of roughed up, kid.

15
00:00:34,995 --> 00:00:35,328
I'll show the second years.

16
00:00:35,411 --> 00:00:36,202
Say cheese.

17
00:00:36,286 --> 00:00:38,328
(laughs)

18
00:00:38,411 --> 00:00:40,911
I got an earful
from the higher-ups

19
00:00:40,995 --> 00:00:43,411
'cause this special-grade
cursed object's still missing.

20
00:00:43,494 --> 00:00:46,286
Thought I'd do a little
sightseeing and stop by.

21
00:00:46,369 --> 00:00:48,745
So, did you find it yet?

22
00:00:48,828 --> 00:00:49,911
(Fushiguro sighs)

23
00:00:49,995 --> 00:00:50,578
-Uh--
-Hmm?

24
00:00:50,661 --> 00:00:53,328
Sorry, but I ate that thing.

25
00:00:55,453 --> 00:00:56,369
Really?

26
00:00:56,453 --> 00:00:58,244
-He did.
-I did.

27
00:00:58,328 --> 00:00:59,328
Hmm?

28
00:01:04,119 --> 00:01:05,119
Hmm.

29
00:01:06,870 --> 00:01:07,703
(laughs)

30
00:01:07,786 --> 00:01:09,369
Damn, it really did
combine with you.

31
00:01:09,453 --> 00:01:11,745
That's hilarious.

32
00:01:11,828 --> 00:01:13,536
Anything weird about your body?

33
00:01:13,619 --> 00:01:15,037
Nah, it seems okay.

34
00:01:15,119 --> 00:01:16,304
Can you swap
with Sukuna at will?

35
00:01:16,328 --> 00:01:17,244
Sukuna?

36
00:01:17,328 --> 00:01:19,578
[Satoru] Yeah,
the curse you ate?

37
00:01:19,661 --> 00:01:23,037
Oh, mm-hmm, yeah,
I think I can do that.

38
00:01:23,161 --> 00:01:25,411
Okay, give us 10 seconds.

39
00:01:25,494 --> 00:01:27,787
Then change right
back into yourself.

40
00:01:27,871 --> 00:01:29,245
Yeah, but..

41
00:01:29,329 --> 00:01:30,579
Don't worry.

42
00:01:30,662 --> 00:01:33,079
I'm way too strong for him.

43
00:01:33,162 --> 00:01:34,662
Megumi, hold onto this for me.

44
00:01:35,412 --> 00:01:36,620
So what is this?

45
00:01:36,704 --> 00:01:38,829
Kikufuku from Kikusuian.

46
00:01:38,912 --> 00:01:41,079
It's Sendai's specialty
and it's super good.

47
00:01:41,162 --> 00:01:42,996
I recommend the
zunda and cream flavor.

48
00:01:43,079 --> 00:01:45,412
[Fushiguro] This guy actually
went and bought souvenirs

49
00:01:45,495 --> 00:01:46,412
while people were
out here dying?

50
00:01:46,495 --> 00:01:48,579
It's no souvenir.

51
00:01:48,662 --> 00:01:51,079
I'll be eating this on the
bullet train ride home.

52
00:01:51,162 --> 00:01:52,454
(thunder crashes)

53
00:01:52,537 --> 00:01:53,787
Look out!

54
00:01:53,871 --> 00:01:54,412
-Kikufuku's just the best.
-(thunder crashes)

55
00:01:54,495 --> 00:01:58,079
(intense music)

56
00:02:04,704 --> 00:02:06,370
I think it's the
whipped cream inside

57
00:02:06,454 --> 00:02:07,722
that really makes
the difference.

58
00:02:07,746 --> 00:02:10,329
(Sukuna growls)

59
00:02:14,704 --> 00:02:17,996
Since my student's watching,
I think I'll show off a little.

60
00:02:18,079 --> 00:02:19,120
Yeah.

61
00:02:19,203 --> 00:02:22,203
(fighters grunting)

62
00:02:22,287 --> 00:02:24,454
Is he unbelievably fast?

63
00:02:24,537 --> 00:02:26,830
No, that's not it.

64
00:02:26,913 --> 00:02:29,788
(fighters grunting)

65
00:02:31,955 --> 00:02:33,455
For crying out loud.

66
00:02:33,538 --> 00:02:36,621
You jujutsu sorcerers are
always such a pain in the ass

67
00:02:36,705 --> 00:02:37,621
in any era.

68
00:02:37,705 --> 00:02:40,580
(building crashing)

69
00:02:41,496 --> 00:02:43,830
(glass shatters)

70
00:02:46,955 --> 00:02:51,496
Though time doesn't really
have much meaning for me.

71
00:02:51,580 --> 00:02:55,039
Seven, eight, nine.

72
00:02:55,121 --> 00:02:56,413
And that should do it.

73
00:02:58,997 --> 00:02:59,997
[Sukuna] Dammit, again?

74
00:03:01,747 --> 00:03:04,330
Why can't I seem to
take over this body?

75
00:03:04,413 --> 00:03:06,455
Who the hell is
this Itadori punk?

76
00:03:09,955 --> 00:03:11,371
[Itadori] Oh, how did it go?

77
00:03:11,455 --> 00:03:13,413
How about that?

78
00:03:13,496 --> 00:03:15,538
So you really can
control that guy?

79
00:03:15,621 --> 00:03:17,705
He's kind of annoying
though to tell the truth

80
00:03:17,788 --> 00:03:20,039
and I keep hearing his voice.

81
00:03:20,121 --> 00:03:21,841
It's a miracle that's
all he's doing to you.

82
00:03:30,622 --> 00:03:32,122
[Megumi] What'd you do to him?

83
00:03:32,205 --> 00:03:33,873
[Satoru] I just knocked him out.

84
00:03:35,164 --> 00:03:37,331
If he isn't possessed by
Sukuna when he wakes up,

85
00:03:37,414 --> 00:03:39,581
then he might have
potential as a vessel.

86
00:03:41,998 --> 00:03:43,581
Now I have a question for you.

87
00:03:43,664 --> 00:03:45,873
What do you think
we should do with him?

88
00:03:47,831 --> 00:03:49,789
Well, even if he is a vessel,

89
00:03:50,289 --> 00:03:53,581
jujutsu regulations
demand Itadori be executed.

90
00:03:54,456 --> 00:03:57,664
However, I don't
want him to die.

91
00:03:59,164 --> 00:04:00,289
Personal?

92
00:04:00,372 --> 00:04:01,497
I suppose.

93
00:04:01,581 --> 00:04:02,372
So can you save him?

94
00:04:02,456 --> 00:04:04,289
(Satoru chuckles)

95
00:04:04,372 --> 00:04:07,372
A request from a
precious student?

96
00:04:07,456 --> 00:04:08,789
Leave it to me.

97
00:04:09,998 --> 00:04:13,622
But the end result
is still your execution.

98
00:04:14,539 --> 00:04:17,622
Your recap doesn't match
with the current events.

99
00:04:17,706 --> 00:04:19,956
Hey, sorry, I did my best.

100
00:04:20,040 --> 00:04:23,372
You still have to die, but I
got your sentence suspended.

101
00:04:23,456 --> 00:04:24,999
What's suspended mean?

102
00:04:25,082 --> 00:04:27,623
You'll wait until
later to kill me?

103
00:04:27,707 --> 00:04:30,041
Yep, I'll just explain
from the top.

104
00:04:30,874 --> 00:04:33,457
This is the same kind of thing
as the cursed object you ate.

105
00:04:33,540 --> 00:04:36,165
There are 20 of these in total.

106
00:04:36,248 --> 00:04:37,999
We possess six of them.

107
00:04:38,082 --> 00:04:38,582
[Itadori] 20?

108
00:04:38,665 --> 00:04:41,123
Oh, each finger and toe?

109
00:04:41,206 --> 00:04:43,832
No, Sukuna has four arms.

110
00:04:47,332 --> 00:04:50,290
(finger exploding)

111
00:04:50,540 --> 00:04:53,540
As you can see, we
can't destroy them.

112
00:04:53,623 --> 00:04:55,999
The curse is that powerful

113
00:04:56,082 --> 00:04:57,558
and the curse grows
stronger every day.

114
00:04:57,582 --> 00:05:01,540
So our modern-day jujutsu
seals just aren't keeping up.

115
00:05:01,623 --> 00:05:02,957
That's where you come in.

116
00:05:03,457 --> 00:05:07,498
When you die, the curse
inside you will die as well.

117
00:05:07,582 --> 00:05:10,623
You see, our elders are cowards.

118
00:05:10,707 --> 00:05:12,957
They're demanding
we kill you right away.

119
00:05:14,540 --> 00:05:16,665
But that would be a
waste, wouldn't you say?

120
00:05:16,749 --> 00:05:18,290
-A waste?
-See,

121
00:05:18,373 --> 00:05:20,206
there's no assurance
another vessel capable

122
00:05:20,290 --> 00:05:23,041
of handling Sukuna
will ever be born again,

123
00:05:23,123 --> 00:05:25,166
so here's what I
proposed to them.

124
00:05:26,374 --> 00:05:28,666
Since they've already
decided to execute you,

125
00:05:28,750 --> 00:05:30,000
why not wait until after

126
00:05:30,083 --> 00:05:32,458
you've absorbed all
of Sukuna to do it?

127
00:05:32,541 --> 00:05:34,042
And the higher-ups agreed.

128
00:05:34,124 --> 00:05:35,684
So now, you have
two options before you.

129
00:05:37,916 --> 00:05:42,042
You can die here and now or
gather all the parts of Sukuna,

130
00:05:42,124 --> 00:05:44,124
absorb them and then die.

131
00:05:47,791 --> 00:05:50,791
(Opening Theme Music)

132
00:06:02,750 --> 00:06:06,541
(singing in Japanese)

133
00:07:22,418 --> 00:07:24,960
(person knocking)

134
00:07:25,044 --> 00:07:26,126
[Sasaki] Itadori.

135
00:07:26,209 --> 00:07:27,209
Hi.

136
00:07:28,835 --> 00:07:29,918
Hello, Sasaki.

137
00:07:30,002 --> 00:07:31,251
How's Iguchi doing?

138
00:07:33,668 --> 00:07:34,960
Well, the doctors say

139
00:07:35,044 --> 00:07:37,126
there's nothing
seriously wrong with him,

140
00:07:37,209 --> 00:07:39,960
but he still hasn't
regained consciousness

141
00:07:40,044 --> 00:07:42,209
and this whole thing's my fault.

142
00:07:42,293 --> 00:07:45,918
I asked him to come to
the school and that night...

143
00:07:47,418 --> 00:07:48,543
(sobs)

144
00:07:48,626 --> 00:07:51,835
I know you won't believe
it, but we got attacked.

145
00:07:51,918 --> 00:07:55,002
By some weird scary monster.

146
00:07:55,085 --> 00:07:58,002
And it captured both of us.

147
00:07:58,085 --> 00:07:59,002
I do believe you

148
00:07:59,085 --> 00:08:00,686
'cause I know that
wasn't a monster exactly.

149
00:08:00,710 --> 00:08:02,960
It was a curse.

150
00:08:03,044 --> 00:08:04,044
Huh?

151
00:08:05,710 --> 00:08:08,002
That finger was a
special-grade cursed object.

152
00:08:08,085 --> 00:08:09,644
It has the power to
draw other curses to it

153
00:08:09,668 --> 00:08:12,335
and make them stronger.

154
00:08:12,418 --> 00:08:15,002
So none of what happened
here was your fault.

155
00:08:15,085 --> 00:08:17,918
It was mine for giving it
to you in the first place.

156
00:08:19,085 --> 00:08:19,918
(soft piano music)

157
00:08:20,002 --> 00:08:24,669
So I'm sorry, but
it'll be all right.

158
00:08:24,753 --> 00:08:28,003
Someone who can fix
Iguchi will be here tomorrow.

159
00:08:28,086 --> 00:08:29,086
Itadori?

160
00:08:30,461 --> 00:08:32,919
Sorry, Sasaki, but I have
somewhere I have to be.

161
00:08:35,294 --> 00:08:36,294
Ba-bye.

162
00:08:46,586 --> 00:08:47,045
[Satoru] Who passed away?

163
00:08:47,127 --> 00:08:48,878
[Itadori] My grandpa,

164
00:08:48,961 --> 00:08:51,294
although he was more
like a father to me.

165
00:08:51,377 --> 00:08:52,252
[Satoru] I see.

166
00:08:52,336 --> 00:08:54,669
Sorry it had to happen
at a time like this.

167
00:08:57,294 --> 00:08:59,878
So, have you decided
what you want to do?

168
00:09:01,502 --> 00:09:02,854
[Itadori] Are
casualties like these

169
00:09:02,878 --> 00:09:04,544
from curses pretty common?

170
00:09:05,794 --> 00:09:08,086
This one was a rather
exceptional case,

171
00:09:08,169 --> 00:09:11,086
but in terms of damage,
it happens all the time.

172
00:09:11,169 --> 00:09:12,687
It's a good night when
someone dies a normal death

173
00:09:12,711 --> 00:09:15,127
after encountering a curse.

174
00:09:19,502 --> 00:09:21,920
Finding a body
that's torn to pieces

175
00:09:22,004 --> 00:09:24,337
is actually one of
the better outcomes.

176
00:09:27,754 --> 00:09:29,628
If you plan to hunt down Sukuna,

177
00:09:29,712 --> 00:09:32,795
you're going to witness
some gruesome stuff

178
00:09:34,337 --> 00:09:38,253
and I can't guarantee you
won't end up that way yourself.

179
00:09:38,337 --> 00:09:41,378
So, I guess you can
choose which hell you want.

180
00:09:50,378 --> 00:09:53,046
[Grandpa] You're a strong
kid, so try to help others.

181
00:10:00,378 --> 00:10:02,837
[Itadori] If all the parts
of Sukuna were gone,

182
00:10:02,920 --> 00:10:04,253
would it really help?

183
00:10:06,170 --> 00:10:08,754
Would there be fewer people
getting harmed by curses?

184
00:10:10,378 --> 00:10:11,462
Yes, of course.

185
00:10:19,629 --> 00:10:21,755
So have you got that finger?

186
00:10:26,588 --> 00:10:28,504
Looking at it again
here in broad daylight,

187
00:10:28,588 --> 00:10:30,212
it's pretty disgusting.

188
00:10:36,421 --> 00:10:37,338
(swallows)

189
00:10:37,421 --> 00:10:39,005
Okay, that's the second one.

190
00:10:39,088 --> 00:10:41,171
One tenth of the whole.

191
00:10:41,254 --> 00:10:42,838
I wonder what's going to happen.

192
00:10:46,963 --> 00:10:52,005
-(Itadori gagging)
-(Sukuna growling)

193
00:10:56,921 --> 00:10:59,838
(Itadori chuckles)

194
00:11:02,088 --> 00:11:03,338
Blech.

195
00:11:03,421 --> 00:11:04,504
So gross.

196
00:11:04,588 --> 00:11:06,546
I mean, so gross it's funny.

197
00:11:06,629 --> 00:11:08,005
[Satoru] (chuckles) There.

198
00:11:08,088 --> 00:11:10,671
It's not just a physical
tolerance that he has.

199
00:11:10,755 --> 00:11:14,463
He can fight off Sukuna's
attempts to take over.

200
00:11:14,546 --> 00:11:16,421
We haven't seen someone
with talent like this

201
00:11:16,504 --> 00:11:18,922
-in 1,000 years.
-What's wrong?

202
00:11:19,006 --> 00:11:20,964
-(rock music)
-Oh, nothing at all.

203
00:11:21,048 --> 00:11:23,547
I take it this means
you've made up your mind.

204
00:11:23,630 --> 00:11:24,756
Chosen your fate?

205
00:11:25,922 --> 00:11:28,213
Not at all.

206
00:11:28,297 --> 00:11:30,922
I still don't understand
why I have to be executed,

207
00:11:31,006 --> 00:11:33,756
but I know I can't
just do nothing.

208
00:11:34,089 --> 00:11:36,380
Grandpa, that last
request of yours

209
00:11:36,464 --> 00:11:38,672
is going to be
a pain in the ass.

210
00:11:39,922 --> 00:11:41,065
I'll eat every part of Sukuna.

211
00:11:41,089 --> 00:11:43,255
After that, I don't care.

212
00:11:44,756 --> 00:11:46,839
As far as how I'm gonna
die, I've already decided.

213
00:11:46,922 --> 00:11:51,714
My guy, I love
finding guys like you.

214
00:11:51,797 --> 00:11:52,839
A fun time in hell awaits.

215
00:11:52,922 --> 00:11:56,422
Make sure you're packed
by the end of the day.

216
00:11:56,505 --> 00:11:57,964
Am I going somewhere?

217
00:11:58,048 --> 00:11:59,213
Tokyo.

218
00:11:59,297 --> 00:12:00,213
Fushiguro!

219
00:12:00,297 --> 00:12:01,422
Looking good, brother.

220
00:12:01,505 --> 00:12:03,422
You think this is looking good?

221
00:12:03,505 --> 00:12:04,048
Anyway, here's the deal.

222
00:12:04,130 --> 00:12:05,964
You're going to the school

223
00:12:06,048 --> 00:12:08,089
for jujutsu sorcerers
that I attend.

224
00:12:08,172 --> 00:12:09,172
Huh?

225
00:12:09,672 --> 00:12:12,964
Tokyo Metropolitan Jujutsu
Technical High School.

226
00:12:14,505 --> 00:12:17,715
By the way, you'll be one
of only three first years there.

227
00:12:17,798 --> 00:12:18,798
Only three?

228
00:12:19,882 --> 00:12:22,798
(bird squawking)

229
00:12:27,798 --> 00:12:29,049
Okay, I'm heading out.

230
00:12:29,131 --> 00:12:30,923
Goodbye, Grandpa.

231
00:12:35,173 --> 00:12:37,256
This is really deep
in the mountains.

232
00:12:37,340 --> 00:12:38,465
Are we still even in Tokyo?

233
00:12:38,548 --> 00:12:41,298
[Satoru] This is what the
outskirts of Tokyo looks like.

234
00:12:41,381 --> 00:12:42,298
[Itadori] Where's Fushiguro?

235
00:12:42,381 --> 00:12:43,899
[Satoru] He's being
treated by a sorcerer

236
00:12:43,923 --> 00:12:47,256
and at the moment,
he's fast asleep.

237
00:12:47,340 --> 00:12:51,256
Tokyo Metropolitan Jujutsu
Technical High School.

238
00:12:51,340 --> 00:12:54,340
It's one of only two
jujutsu educational facilities.

239
00:12:55,506 --> 00:12:56,631
As a sort of cover,

240
00:12:56,715 --> 00:12:59,465
it's known as a
private religious school.

241
00:12:59,548 --> 00:13:02,465
Many jujutsu sorcerers
continue to use it as a base

242
00:13:02,548 --> 00:13:04,715
after graduation,
so it's a pillar

243
00:13:04,798 --> 00:13:07,923
of the jujutsu community,
not just in education,

244
00:13:08,007 --> 00:13:10,840
but for support and
mediation in missions.

245
00:13:10,923 --> 00:13:12,965
Anyway, you're about
to have an interview

246
00:13:13,049 --> 00:13:14,965
with the Principal.

247
00:13:15,049 --> 00:13:16,131
[Itadori] The Principal?

248
00:13:16,214 --> 00:13:17,341
Screw this up

249
00:13:17,424 --> 00:13:19,026
and he could turn you down
for admission just like that.

250
00:13:19,050 --> 00:13:20,966
Huh?

251
00:13:21,050 --> 00:13:22,883
And what happens then,
immediate execution?

252
00:13:22,966 --> 00:13:25,299
What's this?

253
00:13:25,382 --> 00:13:27,966
So you're not the boss?

254
00:13:28,050 --> 00:13:31,174
Any hierarchy other
than strength is worthless.

255
00:13:31,257 --> 00:13:33,174
(Itadori yells)

256
00:13:33,257 --> 00:13:34,549
I'm sorry about that.

257
00:13:34,632 --> 00:13:36,050
Sometimes he just does that.

258
00:13:36,132 --> 00:13:38,132
What an amusing
body you have now.

259
00:13:38,215 --> 00:13:41,050
I do owe you a big favor though.

260
00:13:41,132 --> 00:13:43,299
Once I make this
punk's body my own,

261
00:13:43,382 --> 00:13:45,674
you'll be the first one I kill.

262
00:13:45,758 --> 00:13:48,841
It's my honor to be
targeted by Sukuna himself.

263
00:13:49,549 --> 00:13:50,382
This guy is really that famous?

264
00:13:50,466 --> 00:13:54,632
Ryoumen Sukuna is
an imaginary fierce god

265
00:13:54,716 --> 00:13:56,924
with four arms and two faces.

266
00:13:57,008 --> 00:14:00,841
But he once existed as
an actual human being,

267
00:14:00,924 --> 00:14:03,549
although it was over
a thousand years ago.

268
00:14:03,632 --> 00:14:05,716
In the golden age of jujutsu,

269
00:14:05,799 --> 00:14:07,716
sorcerers gathered
all their might

270
00:14:07,799 --> 00:14:10,132
to challenge him and failed.

271
00:14:10,215 --> 00:14:11,924
Crowned with
the title of Sukuna,

272
00:14:12,008 --> 00:14:14,215
we couldn't even
destroy his grave wax

273
00:14:14,299 --> 00:14:16,925
as he traversed the ages
after death as a cursed object.

274
00:14:17,009 --> 00:14:20,842
Without a doubt, he
is the king of curses.

275
00:14:21,925 --> 00:14:24,051
[Itadori] Who's
stronger, him or you?

276
00:14:24,133 --> 00:14:26,925
[Satoru] Well, if Sukuna
regained all his power,

277
00:14:27,009 --> 00:14:29,009
he might cause
me a little trouble.

278
00:14:29,092 --> 00:14:31,051
But would you lose?

279
00:14:32,300 --> 00:14:33,300
I would win.

280
00:14:40,175 --> 00:14:42,550
You're late, Satoru.

281
00:14:43,175 --> 00:14:45,092
Eight minutes late.

282
00:14:46,133 --> 00:14:50,133
As usual, not quite
enough to chastise you for.

283
00:14:50,216 --> 00:14:52,425
I told you, fix that habit.

284
00:14:52,508 --> 00:14:55,592
That old dude's
making cute things?

285
00:14:55,675 --> 00:14:57,425
If it's not enough
to chastise me for,

286
00:14:57,508 --> 00:14:58,633
then don't chastise.

287
00:14:58,717 --> 00:15:00,967
Besides, you're just sitting
around making dolls anyway,

288
00:15:01,051 --> 00:15:03,051
so what's eight minutes?

289
00:15:03,133 --> 00:15:06,425
Principal Masamichi Yaga.

290
00:15:06,508 --> 00:15:08,133
This is the boy?

291
00:15:08,216 --> 00:15:09,051
Yuuji Itadori.

292
00:15:09,133 --> 00:15:10,967
I'm into girls like
Jennifer Lawrence.

293
00:15:11,051 --> 00:15:12,967
This is an honor.

294
00:15:13,051 --> 00:15:14,675
[Principal] What
are you here for?

295
00:15:15,176 --> 00:15:16,217
An interview?

296
00:15:16,301 --> 00:15:19,093
But why Jujutsu Tech?

297
00:15:19,343 --> 00:15:21,093
To learn jujutsu?

298
00:15:21,176 --> 00:15:23,010
I mean beyond that.

299
00:15:23,093 --> 00:15:26,134
What do you hope to find
once you've studied curses

300
00:15:26,217 --> 00:15:29,926
and learned the art
of exorcizing them?

301
00:15:30,885 --> 00:15:32,384
Well, I suppose,

302
00:15:33,551 --> 00:15:35,801
I'm going to collect all
the fingers of Sukuna.

303
00:15:35,885 --> 00:15:37,426
Can't just leave
them all out there.

304
00:15:37,509 --> 00:15:38,926
-Why not?
-Hmm?

305
00:15:40,551 --> 00:15:42,676
People you'll never
know die every day

306
00:15:42,760 --> 00:15:44,259
due to crime,
accidents, and diseases.

307
00:15:44,343 --> 00:15:47,176
It's just the natural
course of life.

308
00:15:47,259 --> 00:15:48,176
Here he goes again.

309
00:15:48,259 --> 00:15:50,093
But you're telling me
you can't overlook it

310
00:15:50,176 --> 00:15:53,259
when that death is
caused by a curse?

311
00:15:53,343 --> 00:15:55,634
It was someone's
dying request of me.

312
00:15:55,718 --> 00:15:57,676
And I don't care
about the details.

313
00:15:57,760 --> 00:15:59,718
I just want to save who I can.

314
00:15:59,801 --> 00:16:01,551
Hmm, dying wish?

315
00:16:02,801 --> 00:16:04,509
You're saying
you'll fight curses

316
00:16:04,593 --> 00:16:06,968
just because someone
else told you to do that?

317
00:16:07,926 --> 00:16:09,301
Insufficient.

318
00:16:09,384 --> 00:16:11,176
(Itadori gasps)

319
00:16:11,259 --> 00:16:14,969
(creature growls)

320
00:16:15,053 --> 00:16:16,510
That's not a doll.

321
00:16:16,594 --> 00:16:17,177
It's alive.

322
00:16:17,260 --> 00:16:19,469
In a way.

323
00:16:19,552 --> 00:16:20,719
They're corpses.

324
00:16:20,802 --> 00:16:23,344
Dolls that I've
infused with my curse.

325
00:16:23,427 --> 00:16:25,135
(Itadori gasps)

326
00:16:25,218 --> 00:16:27,177
(Itadori grunts)

327
00:16:33,385 --> 00:16:35,218
[Itadori] That's
one hell of a doll.

328
00:16:37,427 --> 00:16:41,260
A person's true nature
reveals itself during a crisis.

329
00:16:41,344 --> 00:16:44,594
I'll keep attacking you until
I get an acceptable answer.

330
00:16:46,469 --> 00:16:48,344
Look, man, it wasn't
just someone else.

331
00:16:48,427 --> 00:16:51,218
It was my grandfather's
dying request.

332
00:16:51,302 --> 00:16:54,177
(grunts)

333
00:17:02,094 --> 00:17:03,094
Where is it?

334
00:17:04,969 --> 00:17:07,094
(grunts)

335
00:17:09,969 --> 00:17:12,011
Family's still just
someone else.

336
00:17:12,302 --> 00:17:14,303
(doll squeaking)

337
00:17:18,428 --> 00:17:20,720
[Itadori] All
right, it's a doll,

338
00:17:20,803 --> 00:17:22,762
so it doesn't get
hurt or scared.

339
00:17:22,845 --> 00:17:25,136
A jujutsu sorcerer
constantly faces death

340
00:17:25,219 --> 00:17:27,762
and not just their own death.

341
00:17:27,845 --> 00:17:29,285
Sometimes you must
ignore the victims

342
00:17:29,345 --> 00:17:32,303
and rend the flesh from those
who the curse has murdered.

343
00:17:33,303 --> 00:17:35,928
It's an unpleasant job.

344
00:17:36,012 --> 00:17:37,553
You have to be highly motivated

345
00:17:37,636 --> 00:17:39,386
and perhaps a little
crazy to handle it.

346
00:17:39,470 --> 00:17:43,054
You'd do this because
someone else told you to?

347
00:17:43,136 --> 00:17:44,386
Don't make me laugh.

348
00:17:44,470 --> 00:17:45,595
It would be more believable

349
00:17:45,678 --> 00:17:48,219
if you said you were doing it
to postpone your execution.

350
00:17:48,303 --> 00:17:49,345
Oh, screw you.

351
00:17:49,428 --> 00:17:51,054
-I--
-And tell me this.

352
00:17:51,136 --> 00:17:52,195
Are you going to blame
your poor grandfather

353
00:17:52,219 --> 00:17:55,136
when you get
killed by a curse too?

354
00:17:58,136 --> 00:17:59,428
Damn, old man.

355
00:17:59,511 --> 00:18:01,845
You say some
pretty harsh things.

356
00:18:01,928 --> 00:18:05,095
Teaching is making
people realize truths.

357
00:18:05,178 --> 00:18:07,511
That's right, I guess.

358
00:18:08,887 --> 00:18:10,970
(grunts)

359
00:18:11,887 --> 00:18:13,971
(grunts)

360
00:18:14,512 --> 00:18:16,596
[Principal] It's not easy

361
00:18:16,679 --> 00:18:19,262
to imagine how you'll
feel on the verge of death.

362
00:18:19,346 --> 00:18:23,055
However, I can say
one thing for certain.

363
00:18:23,137 --> 00:18:24,055
At the rate you're going,

364
00:18:24,137 --> 00:18:26,471
you might end up cursing
your beloved grandfather

365
00:18:26,554 --> 00:18:27,429
for his dying wish.

366
00:18:27,512 --> 00:18:30,971
Jujutsu sorcerers
never die without regret,

367
00:18:31,055 --> 00:18:32,429
so I'll ask you just once more.

368
00:18:32,512 --> 00:18:36,846
Why have you come
here to Jujutsu Tech?

369
00:18:36,929 --> 00:18:37,763
(melancholy music)

370
00:18:37,846 --> 00:18:40,262
As a kid, I was always
better than most

371
00:18:40,346 --> 00:18:42,637
in sports and in fights,

372
00:18:42,721 --> 00:18:46,346
but never once did I think
this is something only I can do.

373
00:18:46,429 --> 00:18:47,429
Never.

374
00:18:48,554 --> 00:18:51,387
(grunts)

375
00:18:53,763 --> 00:18:57,137
Consuming Sukuna is
something only I can do.

376
00:18:57,220 --> 00:18:59,220
So even if I could
escape my death sentence

377
00:18:59,304 --> 00:19:01,554
and run away from
this responsibility,

378
00:19:02,387 --> 00:19:04,137
then someday I'd be eating food,

379
00:19:04,220 --> 00:19:06,013
taking a bath, or reading manga

380
00:19:07,220 --> 00:19:09,637
and the moment
I stopped to think,

381
00:19:09,721 --> 00:19:12,305
I'd go, "Oh, I bet
that right now

382
00:19:12,388 --> 00:19:15,930
"somewhere out there, someone
is dying because of Sukuna."

383
00:19:16,764 --> 00:19:18,638
But that doesn't concern me.

384
00:19:18,722 --> 00:19:20,638
It's certainly not my fault.

385
00:19:20,722 --> 00:19:22,680
You expect me
to tell myself that?

386
00:19:22,764 --> 00:19:25,347
-(rock music)
-Well, I refuse to do that.

387
00:19:26,305 --> 00:19:28,513
I don't know how I'll
feel when I'm dying,

388
00:19:28,597 --> 00:19:32,347
but I won't regret
the way I lived.

389
00:19:36,014 --> 00:19:38,305
Satoru, show him
to his dorm room.

390
00:19:38,388 --> 00:19:42,347
Be sure to explain the security
arrangements to him as well.

391
00:19:44,972 --> 00:19:45,430
You're admitted.

392
00:19:45,513 --> 00:19:47,388
Welcome to Jujutsu Tech.

393
00:19:50,638 --> 00:19:53,680
(Itadori yells)

394
00:19:53,764 --> 00:19:56,388
Sorry, I forgot to
release the curse.

395
00:19:58,597 --> 00:20:00,056
[Itadori] Whoa!

396
00:20:00,138 --> 00:20:01,221
This place is huge.

397
00:20:01,305 --> 00:20:03,889
All the second and third
years are out at the moment,

398
00:20:03,972 --> 00:20:05,323
but you'll meet
them all soon enough.

399
00:20:05,347 --> 00:20:08,138
There aren't many of them.

400
00:20:08,221 --> 00:20:11,723
You know, there's no real
reason for you to go fight at all.

401
00:20:11,806 --> 00:20:14,098
Fushiguro and I could
retrieve Sukuna's fingers

402
00:20:14,181 --> 00:20:16,222
while you just stay
here and chill out.

403
00:20:16,473 --> 00:20:19,723
Yeah, nice try, guy.

404
00:20:19,806 --> 00:20:21,681
I said I'd do it and I will.

405
00:20:22,639 --> 00:20:23,639
Hey, dude.

406
00:20:23,681 --> 00:20:25,181
Though I gotta say,

407
00:20:25,264 --> 00:20:26,449
hanging out until Fushiguro
comes back all beat up

408
00:20:26,473 --> 00:20:30,389
just to bring me a finger,
that would be funny.

409
00:20:30,473 --> 00:20:32,431
Yeah, but you wouldn't
have refused to fight.

410
00:20:32,514 --> 00:20:33,556
I already knew that.

411
00:20:33,639 --> 00:20:35,431
Huh, that was a test?

412
00:20:37,848 --> 00:20:39,931
If the fingers were
that easy to find,

413
00:20:40,015 --> 00:20:43,015
don't you think we'd have
collected them all already?

414
00:20:43,098 --> 00:20:44,365
Some have a presence
that's overwhelming.

415
00:20:44,389 --> 00:20:46,765
Some keep very quiet

416
00:20:46,848 --> 00:20:49,931
and some have already been
absorbed by a curse spirit.

417
00:20:50,015 --> 00:20:52,348
These are the challenges
we've dealt with

418
00:20:52,431 --> 00:20:54,973
when it comes to
searching for them.

419
00:20:55,057 --> 00:20:57,348
But at last we have you.

420
00:20:57,431 --> 00:20:59,598
The Sukuna within you
will try to regain his power

421
00:20:59,681 --> 00:21:02,765
and that will lead
us to the fingers.

422
00:21:02,848 --> 00:21:06,431
You're both vessel and
locator, our very own radar.

423
00:21:06,514 --> 00:21:10,349
So you see, we won't
get very far without you.

424
00:21:10,432 --> 00:21:13,058
Are you sure he's going
to be that cooperative?

425
00:21:13,682 --> 00:21:16,474
Oh, I think we can come to
a win-win agreement there.

426
00:21:16,557 --> 00:21:18,640
[Fushiguro] You're next door.

427
00:21:18,724 --> 00:21:19,349
Hey, Fushiguro.

428
00:21:19,432 --> 00:21:22,140
Wow, you look all better now.

429
00:21:22,223 --> 00:21:23,533
There's lots of other
empty rooms, you know?

430
00:21:23,557 --> 00:21:26,932
Sure, but isn't it better
to have some company?

431
00:21:27,016 --> 00:21:28,140
I thought it'd be good.

432
00:21:28,223 --> 00:21:29,515
Classes and missions are enough.

433
00:21:29,599 --> 00:21:31,140
This is not welcome.

434
00:21:31,223 --> 00:21:33,557
Whoa, it's so organized in here.

435
00:21:33,640 --> 00:21:35,016
Back off.

436
00:21:35,099 --> 00:21:37,390
I just told you,
you're not welcome.

437
00:21:37,474 --> 00:21:38,390
Ha, friends already.

438
00:21:38,474 --> 00:21:42,307
And together we're
heading out tomorrow.

439
00:21:42,390 --> 00:21:45,390
We're going to go pick up
the third and final first-year.

440
00:21:46,265 --> 00:21:47,849
(train horn)

441
00:21:49,390 --> 00:21:52,307
[PA] The train bound
for Tokyo is now arriving.

442
00:21:52,390 --> 00:21:53,790
Please stand behind
the yellow line.

443
00:21:55,640 --> 00:21:56,515
(Nobara grunts)

444
00:21:56,599 --> 00:22:00,349
Four hours and I'm
still only in Morioka,

445
00:22:00,432 --> 00:22:02,016
but at least I can finally kiss

446
00:22:02,099 --> 00:22:03,891
that damn countryside goodbye.

447
00:22:06,599 --> 00:22:09,516
And I'll be in Tokyo
by this afternoon.

448
00:22:09,600 --> 00:22:11,516
What should I do
if I get scouted?

449
00:22:12,558 --> 00:22:13,725
Like by Stardust?

450
00:22:15,600 --> 00:22:18,558
(Closing Theme music)

451
00:22:22,767 --> 00:22:26,558
(singing in Japanese)

452
00:23:45,601 --> 00:23:50,642
(ominous music)

